course: dictionary
lesson: 15186
title: Seatbelts keep you safe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A seatbelt is a strong belt in a car, bus or plane. It holds you in your seat. «Always fasten your seatbelt before the car moves.» The words before the car moves tell you this is about safety, so a seatbelt must be something that keeps you in place.
explain: «Buckle up, everyone, we are leaving now.» Buckle up is another way to say fasten your seatbelt. When you hear it, click the belt across your body so it is locked.
explain: Children often sit on a booster seat, which lifts them up. «The booster seat helps the seatbelt sit low on your hips and across your chest.» The seatbelt has to fit the body it is protecting, so the booster helps.
fact: A seatbelt is a strong belt that holds you in your seat.
fact: Seatbelts keep you safe in a crash or a sudden stop.
fact: Fasten your seatbelt means do up the belt so it is locked.
fact: «Seatbelt» is a noun, and you can also write it as two words: seat belt.
fact: In many countries, wearing a seatbelt is the law, for drivers and passengers.
exercise: «Always fasten your seatbelt before the car moves.» What is a seatbelt? | A small wheel on a bike | *A strong belt that holds you in your seat | A sort of hat for sunny days | A bag for carrying your shoes
exercise: Dad says, «Buckle up, everyone!» What does buckle up mean? | Sing a song loudly | Take off your shoes | *Fasten your seatbelt | Get out and run
exercise: Why do some children sit on a booster seat in the car? | To make the car go faster | *So the seatbelt fits them properly | Because booster seats are for sleeping | So they can see the television
test: Which job does a seatbelt do? | It is a place to keep your snacks | *It keeps you in your seat during a crash or sudden stop | It makes the car go faster | It cleans the windows
test: Find the phrase that means fasten your seatbelt. | Car door | *Buckle up | Seatbelt sign | Booster seat
exam: «The seatbelt is the law, so always wear it.» What does this tell you? | Seatbelts are only for planes | Seatbelts are only for grown-ups | *You must wear it, because it keeps you safe | You may wear it if you like
